Lecture 2
Maven & JavaFX Setup
  Learn how Maven automates project builds and handles Java dependencies without manual downloads.
  Understand how to run Maven JavaFX projects within IntelliJ IDEA.
  Get familiar with the default file layout of a Maven-based JavaFX application.
JavaFX Shape Rendering & Styling
  Know how to instantiate and render basic 2D shapes, such as Rectangle.
  Differentiate between solid fill and outline-only rendering.
  Use setFill() for inner color and setStroke() for outline color.
  Apply Color.TRANSPARENT to create hollow shapes.
  Control border thickness using setStrokeWidth().
Shape Positioning & Sizing
  Use setLayoutX() and setLayoutY() to place elements on the screen.
  Set shape dimensions using setWidth() and setHeight().
  Grasp how adjustments to layout and dimensions alter object rendering.
Practical Exercise
  Build a simple Maven-backed JavaFX application.
  Draw a standard square using the Rectangle class.
  Convert the square into a hollow shape with a defined border color and width.
  Tweak sizing, placement, and stroke settings to observe graphical changes.
